[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2814049223","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99821#issuecomment-2814049223","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99821","id":2814049223,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nuvvH","user":{"login":"Nallebeorn","id":7013489,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTM0ODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7013489?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn","html_url":"https://github.com/Nallebeorn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-17T21:21:08Z","updated_at":"2025-04-17T21:21:08Z","body":"Reproducible with the linked online MRP in Chrome and Firefox on a Google Pixel 8a (GPU: ARM Mali-G715). Not reproducible in Chrome or Samsung Internet on my Samsung Galaxy Tab S9 (GPU: Qualcomm Adreno 740), nor on an iPhone 13.\n\nBoth of my Android devices have fairly recent GPUs from around the same time that are supposed to support OpenGL ES 3.2. Interestingly, the Amazon Fire HD 10 mentioned by OP also seems to have a Mali GPU. I can find some other mentions of similar errors, e.g. https://www.reddit.com/r/opengl/comments/zs60wi/es_gl_no_default_precision_defined_for_variable/, so this could be a driver bug on certain devices.\n\nI can also confirm the error message, I get same one in Chrome (retrieved via USB debugging). As far as I can tell the generated shader code line causing problems is completely valid in OpenGL ES 3 (i.e. WebGL 2), but possibly relevant is that this type of array initialization _wasn't_ supported in OpenGL ES 2 (WebGL 1.0)\n\n@AThousandShips \n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2814049223/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2822022552","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99821#issuecomment-2822022552","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99821","id":2822022552,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oNKWY","user":{"login":"futureradius","id":2284725,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyODQ3MjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2284725?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/futureradius","html_url":"https://github.com/futureradius","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futureradius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futureradius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futureradius/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futureradius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futureradius/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futureradius/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futureradius/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futureradius/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futureradius/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T17:34:35Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T17:34:35Z","body":"Hey, i had an issue with just exporting anything to web, leading to every texture being black. I tried around extensively and a sure fire way to avoid the problem was to reimport everything with VRAM Texture Compression turned off, imported als Lossless or lossy.. even the baked lightmaps..\n\nVram for mobile and for desktop had the same issues, is this related? or should i file another report?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2822022552/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2822196728","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99821#issuecomment-2822196728","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99821","id":2822196728,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oN034","user":{"login":"Nallebeorn","id":7013489,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTM0ODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7013489?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn","html_url":"https://github.com/Nallebeorn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T18:51:47Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T18:51:47Z","b